{
    "background_story": "Vance was a charismatic salsa dancer from Havana, Cuba. Growing up in a vibrant Latin American community, he was surrounded by the rhythms and flavors of his heritage. Vance's passion for dance was ignited by his abuela, who taught him the traditional steps of salsa and rumba. As he honed his skills, he became a sought-after performer in local dance troupes and competitions. Vance's love for Latin culture extended beyond dance; he was also an avid student of Spanish literature and history. He spent years mastering the works of Cervantes and Lorca, and even taught Latin American studies at a local university. Vance's infectious energy and dedication to preserving Latin traditions made him a beloved figure in his community, and his dance studio became a hub for cultural exchange and celebration.",
